# L §8.3 Which refusal prints (tally 2.1.1): load takes the files in the order of their full paths, compared by code
# point, whatever order they are given in, and prints the first refusal it meets. b.tally and a.tally, given in that
# order, each have a tab on line 4 (LOAD-PARSE): a.tally's prints (issue #13, T1's synthetic pair, INTERFACE §5).
=== z.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
=== b.tally
part pb
  tally 2

	def x: int = 1
=== a.tally
part pa
  tally 2

	def y: int = 1
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: tab (a.tally:4)
